# Goal 8: Fix pow — wrong output

## Function
- `pow` (double precision)

## Source Files
- C: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/powd.c`
- Rust: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/lib.rs` (wrapper), implementation in `mathd.rs`

## Problem
MISMATCH: pow returns wrong values:
- C:    `pow 0x1p+1 0x1.4p+3 = 0x1p+10`
  (pow(2,10) = 1024 exactly)
- Rust: `pow 0x1p+1 0x1.4p+3 = 0x1.b2d809254afbcp+11`

- C:    `pow -0x1p+1 0x1.8p+1 = -0x1p+3`
  (pow(-2,3) = -8 exactly)
- Rust: `pow -0x1p+1 0x1.8p+1 = -0x1.fffee746db0fcp+5`

Note: pow(2,10) has the same wrong Rust value as exp2(10), suggesting
pow internally uses exp2. Fixing exp2 (Goal 7) may fix pow as well, but
pow should be verified independently.

## What Needs to Change
Compare the Rust pow implementation against the C source in `powd.c`. The
error pattern matches exp2, so likely the same root cause (exp2 bug).
After fixing exp2, re-test pow. If still failing, fix pow's own logic.

## Success Criteria
- `pow(2.0, 10.0)` returns `0x1p+10` (bitwise exact)
- `pow(-2.0, 3.0)` returns `-0x1p+3` (bitwise exact)
